From edd at debian.org  Sun Oct 26 12:55:07 2025
From: edd at debian.org (Dirk Eddelbuettel)
Date: Sun, 26 Oct 2025 07:55:07 -0500
Subject: r-cran-xml2 blocks libxml2 transition
Message-ID: <26878.6699.669473.598982@paul.eddelbuettel.com>

Debian R team:

doko (CC'ed) noticed in autpkg tests that CRAN package xml2 aka r-cran-xml2
fails under the to-be-transitioned-to-testing candidate libxml2-dev 2.15.

Because XML (mine, older) and xml2 (your, newer) are close in name, the
one-char difference was missed and this landed in my lap.

I have reassigned the bug report to you. It would be nice if someone could
pick it up and run with it.

As I know Jeroen upstream (also CC'ed), I also notified him after checking
that the issue appears to not yet be present in the upstream issues (though I
could have missed it), that is at https://github.com/r-lib/xml2/issues/468

I also verified that the suspected simple change fixes it, the diff is in the
upstream issue ticket, and for convenience also below.  I will leave to you
to ponder (maybe together with upstream) if this needs a generalization
relative to the libxml2-dev version which, I presume, one case access from R
as is common.

Cheers, Dirk

diff -ru xml2.orig/tests/testthat/test-xml_write.R xml2/tests/testthat/test-xml_write.R
--- xml2.orig/tests/testthat/test-xml_write.R   2024-12-15 22:16:23.000000000 +0000
+++ xml2/tests/testthat/test-xml_write.R        2025-10-26 12:41:20.380626516 +0000
@@ -126,7 +126,7 @@
   })
   expect_identical(
     readChar(file, 1000L),
-    "<!DOCTYPE html PUBLIC \"-//W3C//DTD HTML 4.0 Transitional//EN\" \"http://www.w3.org/TR/REC-html40/loose.dtd\">\n<html><head>\n<meta http-equiv=\"Content-Type\" content=\"text/html; charset=UTF-8\">\n<title>Foo</title>\n</head></html>\n"
+    "<!DOCTYPE html PUBLIC \"-//W3C//DTD HTML 4.0 Transitional//EN\" \"http://www.w3.org/TR/REC-html40/loose.dtd\">\n<html><head>\n<meta charset=\"UTF-8\">\n<title>Foo</title>\n</head></html>\n"
   )
 })
 
